  m_Name: Sinosauropteryx
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  creatureName: Sinosauroptery
  description: "A smaller than average dinosaur, the Sinosauropteryx (Simon for short)
    is a tiny predator and scavenger, usually feasting on small mammals and reptiles,
    though it won\u2019t turn its nose up at the occasional insect. These dinosaurs
    are covered in tiny fur-like feathers that they need help to groom, leading to
    their social behavior. Simons are a pack species, and their young will imprint
    on whichever parent is the first it sees. This helps the pack to remain bonded
    and coordinate to hunt slightly larger animals for food, such as rabbits.\r\n"
